# ─── API ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL the app fetches from. Leave it unset (or empty) and the app talks to the
# mock API bundled in server/api — same-origin, no backend needed. Point it at a
# real backend when there is one; nothing in the components changes.
#   API_BASE_URL=https://api.thornloefarmsupply.ca/api/
API_BASE_URL=

# ─── Mock API ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Artificial delay added to /api/** so loading states are actually exercised — a
# local handler answering in 1ms hides every skeleton. Unset it and each request
# waits a random 100–200ms; set a number to use exactly that many ms; set 0 to turn
# it off. NOTE: this is not gated to development — a production build honours it too.
MOCK_LATENCY_MS=
